    /// Change an item of the seller's stock
    ///
    /// Changes one item of the seller's stock with a JSON merge patch: a field left out keeps its value, a field set to `null` is cleared (not `name`, `sold`, nor a list: send `[]` to empty a list), a list replaces the whole list. It changes the item in ControlResell only, not its listings on the marketplaces. The amounts are `{amount, currency}` in the item's currency (EUR for a new item; another currency is refused with `422 currency_mismatch`). `photoIds` are files already in the seller's library: another seller's, or an unknown one, is `404 photo_not_found`. A label the seller does not have yet is created. The fields a marketplace asks for are written with the item: `packageSizeId`, `materialIds`, `measurementLength` and `measurementWidth` (centimeters), `enumValues` (the category's enumerated fields, `{enumKey, enumValue}`, one entry per picked value), `attributes` (its free-text fields, `{fieldKey, value}`, one per key) and `customFields` (the seller's own fields, `{fieldId, value}`); each list replaces the item's whole list. A place (`purchasePlaceId`, `sellingPlaceId`) or a custom field of another seller, or an unknown one, is `404 place_not_found` or `404 field_not_found`. `categoryId`, `sizeId` and `state` are ids from 1 (`0` is a 400, `null` clears them). Keys and enumerated values are trimmed and counted in characters (UTF-16 units), 1 to 100 for a key and 1 to 255 for a value; two entries that differ only by case or accents (as the database compares them) are a 400. At most 100 entries per list, and 65,535 bytes (UTF-8) per free-text value. Read back, `enumValues`, `attributes` and `customFields` are sorted by key (then value, or field id), as plain strings (upper case before lower case). Requires `items:write`.
